# Finale of Revelation ({X}{U}{U}) with X = 10 (the boundary) takes the "instead" branch: Bot1 shuffles their graveyard (the
# Black Lotus sacrificed to pay) into their library, draws ten cards, untaps up to five lands and has no maximum hand size for
# the rest of the game (CR 402.2); the spell exiles itself last. It costs 12 mana (Lotus 3, three Moxen, Sol Ring 2, four
# Islands). The untap is a choice, not a target, and the lands need not be Bot1's:
# six chosen is one too many (CR 701.26b, "up to five"); Bot1 untaps three of their own Islands and both Islands Bot2
# tapped on their turn, leaving their fourth Island, the Sol Ring and the Moxen tapped (a Sol Ring is no land). Bot1 holds ten
# cards at the cleanup step and discards none, and the Lotus is back in the library, so the graveyard is empty. The limit is gone
# for the rest of the game, not this turn alone: on turn 9 Bot1 draws an eleventh card and still discards nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Sol Ring
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Island
Island
Island
Island
Finale of Revelation
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

